Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:15:26 -0700
Subject: Prevent overflow of cc::Layer ID's.

Overflowing a 32-bit integer is pathological so just crash.

Fixed: 523554372
Change-Id: Iadc3ce18060cce112f161679f9491d1cc4b2f64b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8301512
Auto-Submit: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Stefan Zager <szager@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Philip Rogers <pdr@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1686872}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y, Chromium 148.0.7778.280):
- Include hunk re-anchored: the branch's layer.cc does not include <cmath>, so
  only <limits> is added. The GetNextLayerId() hunk applied cleanly.

diff --git a/cc/layers/layer.cc b/cc/layers/layer.cc
index bc6103662c35e99f2636353fc5fe1c330af03a2d..b70370a29955e0ef39c11bc1b8c5e56339dfdf21 100644
--- a/cc/layers/layer.cc
+++ b/cc/layers/layer.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <limits>
 #include <string>
 #include <unordered_set>
 #include <utility>
@@ -95,7 +96,9 @@ Layer::LayerTreeInputs::~LayerTreeInputs() = default;
 
 int Layer::GetNextLayerId() {
   // Layer IDs start from 1.
-  return g_next_layer_id.GetNext() + 1;
+  int prev = g_next_layer_id.GetNext();
+  CHECK_LT(prev, std::numeric_limits<int>::max());
+  return prev + 1;
 }
 
 scoped_refptr<Layer> Layer::Create() {
